                       "severity":  "High",
                       "query":  "AzureActivity\n| where ActivityStatusValue =~ \"Success\"\n| where OperationNameValue endswith \"/DELETE\"\n| summarize DeleteCount = count(), TargetResources = make_set(Resource, 25), Operations = make_set(OperationNameValue, 15),\n    StartTime = min(TimeGenerated), EndTime = max(TimeGenerated)\n    by Caller, CallerIpAddress\n| where DeleteCount \u003e= 10\n| extend TimeGenerated = EndTime, Account = Caller, IP = CallerIpAddress",
                       "suppressionDuration":  "PT5H",
                       "suppressionEnabled":  false,
                       "tactics":  [
                                       "Impact"
                                   ],
                       "techniques":  [
                                          "T1485"
                                      ],
                       "displayName":  "Azure - Mass Resource Deletion Burst",
                       "enabled":  true,
                       "description":  "DETECTS\nA single caller successfully deleting ten or more Azure resources within one hour.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nVolume is the signal here. Individual deletions are routine; a burst is characteristic of destructive intent, whether ransomware-adjacent extortion, a disgruntled insider, or a runaway script (MITRE T1485, Data Destruction). Catching the pattern early can stop the deletion mid-sequence.\n\nTRIAGE\n1. Review the resource list to judge scope and business impact.\n2. Confirm whether a decommissioning project or teardown pipeline is running.\n3. Check whether deletions are still in progress. If so, contain the identity immediately rather than completing triage first.\n4. Correlate with a preceding role assignment to the same Caller, which would indicate escalate-then-destroy.\n5. If unauthorized: disable the account, revoke tokens, and begin recovery from IaC.\n\nFALSE POSITIVES\nEnvironment teardown, ephemeral CI/CD, and lab cleanup will trigger this. Tune by excluding pipeline service principals or raising the threshold.\n\nSOURCE\nAzureActivity",
                       "alertRuleTemplateName":  null
                   }
}